    "created_at": "2017-09-01T01:03:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-01T01:03:30Z",
    "body": "It looks like you're trying to use the history state as both an object and a stack at the same time. I feel like this could become confusing on a webpage that heavily uses the history state. I'm also concerned that these changes may affect webpages using the current api. You mention making it feel more like `localStorage`, but why not make it *exactly* like `localStorage` (with the exception of having to stringify everything)? `history.state` and `history.length` could work the same as they do now, and there would be three new functions: `history.setItem`, `history.getItem`, and `history.removeItem`. Setting items this way would not affect `history.state`, so it wouldn't break anything.\r\n\r\nOther potentially relevant discussions: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1454 https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2985",
